6953</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sowers</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Gunsalus</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Halotolerance in <italic>Methanosarcina </italic>spp.: Role of N<sup>&#x003b5;</sup>-acetyl-&#x003b2;-lysine, &#x003b1;-glutamate, glycine betaine, and K<sup>+ </sup>as compatible solutes for osmotic adaptation</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>1995</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>4382</fpage><lpage>4388</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16535193</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>C&#x000e1;novas</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Vargas</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Csonka</surname><given-names>LN</given-names></name><name><surname>Ventosa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nieto</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Synthesis of glycine betaine from exogenous choline in the moderately halophilic bacterium <italic>Halomonas elongata</italic></article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>4095</fpage><lpage>4097</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9758852</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kuhlmann</surname><given-names>AU</given-names></name><name><surname>Bremer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Osmotically regulated synthesis of the compatible solute ectoine in <italic>Bacillus pasteurii </italic>and related <italic>Bacillus </italic>spp</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>772</fpage><lpage>783</lpage><pub-id pub-id-