iven-names></name><name><surname>Warr</surname><given-names>SRC</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>WDP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Organic solute accumulation in in osmotically stressed cyanobacteria</article-title><source>FEMS Microbiol Rev</source><year>1986</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>56</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borowitzka</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The salt relations of marine and halophilic species of the unicellular green alga, <italic>Dunaliella</italic>. The role of glycerol as a compatible solute</article-title><source>Arch Mikrobiol</source><year>1974</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4152062</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Petrovi&#x000e8;</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Gunde-Cimerman</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Plemenita&#x00161;</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cellular responses to environmental salinity in the halophilic black yeast <italic>Hortaea werneckii</italic></article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>665</fpage><lpage>672</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12139614</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scholz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sonnenbichler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sch&#x000e4;fer</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Hens